    "final_assistant_text": "Both changes are applied and verified by re-reading the files. Since the evaluation policy blocks every `run_command` execution, I could not run the suggested unittest suite in this environment, so I verified the behavior by tracing the code.\n\n**Changes made** (only `src/pipeline/`; `README.md` and `tests/` untouched):\n\n1. `src/pipeline/steps.py` — `normalize_step` now strips surrounding `/` characters:\n   ```python\n   return step.strip().strip(\" /\").strip().lower()\n   ```\n   - `normalize_step(\" /Deploy /\")` → `step.strip()` yields `\"/Deploy /\"`, then `.strip(\" /\")` removes the leading `/` and the trailing `/`, yielding `\"Deploy\"` → `\"deploy\"` ✓\n   - `normalize_step(\"a/b\")` → no surrounding slashes, stays `\"a/b\"` ✓\n\n2. `src/pipeline/runner.py` — the inline copy of the rule is gone; `run_step` now imports and delegates to the single canonical rule:\n   ```python\n   from .steps import normalize_step\n\n   def run_step(step: str) -> str:\n       cleaned = normalize_step(step)\n       return f\"ran {cleaned}\"\n   ```\n   So `run_step(\" /Deploy /\")` returns `\"ran deploy\"` ✓\n\nThe `step.strip().lower()` rule now exists in exactly one place: `normalize_step` in `steps.py`.",
